From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:50:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/51] B70-K2: HC down int8 with per-(token, stream) scales
 (B70_HC_DOWN_INT8_STREAM_SCALE, default off)

With B70_HC_DOWN_INT8=1: the combine/norm producers emit int8 + [M,4] scales per
(token, stream); weights int8 per (row, stream); vLLM Triton split-K (exact int32
per split, fixed-order fp32 sum, batch-invariant) feeding the V2 finish+silu (and
the K2 HC up quant). Also B70_K2_HC_CAPTURE_DIR diagnostics dump of HC-down inputs.
K2 producer kernels/tests: ruff format. CPU tests: 63 passed.
